{% set ppm = best.pages_per_min if best else thr.v3.pages_per_minute %}
{% if study %}
<!-- 13 User study -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">Practical value &middot; people in the loop</div>
  <h1>With RedactAgent, people redact faster <i>and</i> miss less</h1>
  <p class="lead">{{ study.participants }} participants each redacted the same six unseen (v3) pages: three by hand, three starting from
    RedactAgent's suggestions (order counterbalanced). Same pixel-level scoring as the benchmark.</p>
  <div class="grid2" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr">
    <table class="t">
      <tr><th>Condition</th><th>Time / page (median)</th><th>Recall</th><th>Precision</th></tr>
      {% for r in study.rows %}
      <tr{% if r.mode == "assisted" %} class="hl"{% endif %}><td>{{ r.label }}</td><td>{{ r.time }}</td><td>{{ r.recall }}</td><td>{{ r.precision }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
    <div>
      <div class="grid2" style="gap:12px">
        <div class="card"><div class="big">{{ study.speedup }}</div><div class="bigl">faster per page with suggestions</div></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="big">{{ study.recall_gain }}</div><div class="bigl">more PII removed than by hand</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:12px"><h3>Reading the result</h3><p>{{ study.note }}</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Small sample; synthetic documents; participants were university students, not records officers. Raw data: eval/results_b70/study.json.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span>RedactAgent &middot; ASUS UGen AI League 2026 &middot; Final</span><span>13</span></div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<!-- 14 Value -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">Practical value &middot; what a hospital gets</div>
  <h1>Less risk, more capacity, and proof for the regulator</h1>
  <p class="lead">Clerical time costs about NT$227 an hour, so the case is not cheaper labour. It is
    <b>fewer leaks</b>, <b>no backlog</b> and <b>evidence</b> &mdash; without data leaving the hospital.</p>
  <div class="grid4" style="margin-top:6px">
    <div class="card"><div class="big">{{ "%.1f"|format(fin.v3.D_agentic.recall*100) }}%</div><div class="bigl">of personal data removed on unseen pages <i>before</i> human review (single human reviewers: 81&nbsp;% in a published study)</div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="big">{{ "{:,.0f}".format(ppm * 60) }}</div><div class="bigl">pages per hour on one 2&times; B70 host, full pipeline incl. the agentic check</div></div>
    {% if triage %}<div class="card"><div class="big">{{ "%.0f"|format(triage.caught*100) }}%</div><div class="bigl">of the remaining misses are on the {{ "%.0f"|format(triage.flagged*100) }}&nbsp;% of pages flagged for full review (risk score or unread ink)</div></div>{% endif %}
    {% if robust_min %}<div class="card"><div class="big">&ge;{{ "%.0f"|format((robust_min*100)|round(0,'floor')) }}%</div><div class="bigl">recall on blurred, low-resolution, fax and skewed scans</div></div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  <table class="t" style="font-size:13.5px;margin-top:16px">
    <tr><th style="width:19%">Who in the hospital</th><th style="width:31%">Their problem</th><th>What RedactAgent gives them</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Records office</b></td><td>Copy requests and research extracts queue up; every page read twice</td><td>Pre-marked pages, a review queue ordered by risk, batch and hot-folder processing</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Privacy officer</b></td><td>Must show the PDPA test &ldquo;cannot identify the person&rdquo; was met</td><td>Purpose policies as files, re-identification risk per page, hash-chained audit from input hash to output hash</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>IRB &amp; researchers</b></td><td>Studies wait for de-identified data</td><td>Research policy: consistent pseudonyms and year-only dates, released after one review</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Hospital IT</b></td><td>No cloud for medical records; no new integration project</td><td>One on-premises appliance, REST API and hot folder (docs/INTEGRATION.md), no per-page fees</td></tr>
  </table>
  <div class="src">Labour cost: MOL occupational wage survey 2025 (clerical support NT$40,000/month). Human recall: Neamatullah et al. 2008 (clinical notes, not our corpus).
    Triage figures from development data (v1 + v2, {{ triage.pages if triage else '' }} pages). Human review stays mandatory for every page.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span>RedactAgent &middot; ASUS UGen AI League 2026 &middot; Final</span><span></span></div>
</section>

